<title>BELGIUM: Fortis Q1 profit up 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Fortis Q1 profit up 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of Ecus, unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		  204   vs  157</p>
<p>    Cons operating profit	  321   vs  243</p>
<p>NOTE - Fortis is a banking and insurance group co-owned by Belgian Fortis AG and Dutch Fortis AMEV.</p>
<p>Results of parent companies as follows:</p>
<p>Fortis AG (in billions of Belgian francs, unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		  3.97  vs  2.73</p>
<p>    Cons net per share (francs)    95  vs    73</p>
<p>    Number of shares (in million) 41.74  vs 37.54</p>
<p>Fortis AMEV (in millions of guilders, unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		   224  vs    171</p>
<p>    Cons net per share (guilders) 1.23 vs   0.94</p>
<p>    Number of shares (in million)   182.79 vs 181.24</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
